   "type": "DOCUMENT",
   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CCM301 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13398 · Decision 932/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 22/08/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CCM301 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13398 · QĐ 932/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 22/08/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>- Attend at least 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>- Actively participate in class activities<br><br>- Fulfill tasks given by instructor after class<br><br>- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Read the textbook in advance<br><br>- Access the course websites (<a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn</a>) for up-to-date information and material of the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>- Attend at least 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>- Actively participate in class activities<br><br>- Fulfill tasks given by instructor after class<br><br>- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Read the textbook in advance<br><br>- Access the course websites (<a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn</a>) for up-to-date information and material of the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (36)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (36)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>QN1.1</td><td>What are the differences among a crisis, a disaster and an incident?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td>QN2.1</td><td>What are the negative or undesirable outcomes of a crisis?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td>QN3. 1</td><td>What are the similarities among 3 below-mentioned models?<br>- Fink’s (1986) four-stage model<br>- Mitroff’s (1994) five-stage model<br>- Basic three-stage model</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>QN4.1</td><td>What dose it mean to say a risk can develop into a crisis?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td>QN5.1</td><td>Could you identify the stages of a crisis of your choice based on 3 distinguished models?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td>QN6.1</td><td>Why bother differentiating between crises and paracrises?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>QN7.1</td><td>What value do you see in the OODA Loop for crisis management and crisis communication?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>QN8.1</td><td>Do you agree or disagree with the idea that a crisis is perceptual?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td>QN9.1</td><td>What are 3 management functions of the Enterprise Risk Management (ERM)?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td>QN10.1</td><td>What dose it mean to say a risk can develop into a crisis?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>11</td><td>QN11.1</td><td>What is reputation? How does it relate to crisis management?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>12</td><td>QN12.1</td><td>What are primary and secondary stakeholders of an enterprise?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>QN13.1</td><td>How can a risk become an issue, an issue become a risk, a risk threaten reputation, or an issue threaten reputation? How do you see these three functions being interrelated?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>QN14.1</td><td>Why should managers bother identifying red flags?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>15</td><td>QN15.1</td><td>Could you list down some issue management sources to scan?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td>QN16.1</td><td>Does it make sense to distinguish between traditional websites and social media, or should we treat all online communication channels and platforms the same?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>17</td><td>QN17.1</td><td>What is the formula to assess each Crisis Threat?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>18</td><td>QN18.1</td><td>How is social media changing crisis prevention efforts?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>19</td><td>QN19.1</td><td>What strategies can be used in response to the stakeholders' challenges?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>20</td><td>QN20.1</td><td>Why could you consider paracrises both risks and opportunities?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>21</td><td>QN21.1</td><td>What barriers are there to getting an accurate diagnosis of an organization’s vulnerabilities? What can be done to overcome those barriers?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>22</td><td>QN22.1</td><td>How to create a crisis portfolio?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>23</td><td>QN23.1</td><td>Why may a Crisis Management Team not be the best place for a CEO during a crisis?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>24</td><td>QN24.1</td><td>What are media-specific tasks of the spokesperson?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>25</td><td>QN25.1</td><td>What are the values of the Crisis Management Plan?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>26</td><td>QN26.1</td><td>What are the main components of a Crisis Management Plan?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>27</td><td>QN27.1</td><td>Why should a team care about mass notification?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>28</td><td>QN28.1</td><td>How might faithholders help an organization in crisis?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>33</td><td>QN33.1</td><td>What factors play a role in developing an appealing crisis frame?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>35</td><td>QN35.1</td><td>What are some common information-processing problems?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>39</td><td>QN39.1</td><td>Why shouldn't an organisation remain silent when a crisis happens?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>42</td><td>QN42.1</td><td>What is the distinctiveness of the Situational Crisis Communication Theory (SCCT)?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>43</td><td>QN43.1</td><td>Could you list down some common crisis communication strategies?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>44</td><td>QN44.1</td><td>What are the dangers associated with using a denial strategy?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>45</td><td>QN45.1</td><td>Why does auto-communication help to unite internal and external crisis communication efforts?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>51</td><td>QN51.1</td><td>Why is an actual crisis a “tremendous opportunity for learning”?</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13398\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13398</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13398\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13398</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
